136
00:06:17,134 --> 00:06:19,773
Divide by zero point zero two five zero

137
00:06:19,934 --> 00:06:23,053
zero: zero point zero four six nine zero

138
00:06:23,294 --> 00:06:24,333
moles per litre.

139
00:06:24,814 --> 00:06:27,293
Using one to one doubles the answer.

140
00:06:28,500 --> 00:06:29,140
Last one.

141
00:06:29,700 --> 00:06:32,660
Two flasks each hold twenty five point zero

142
00:06:32,820 --> 00:06:35,940
zero millilitres of acid at zero point one

143
00:06:36,100 --> 00:06:39,300
zero zero moles per litre: hydrochloric acid in

144
00:06:39,380 --> 00:06:42,740
flask A, and ethanoic acid in flask B.

145
00:06:43,380 --> 00:06:46,020
Each is titrated with zero point one zero

146
00:06:46,140 --> 00:06:48,740
zero moles per litre sodium hydroxide.

147
00:06:49,380 --> 00:06:51,700
Predict the volume needed to reach the equivalence

148
00:06:51,780 --> 00:06:54,820
point in each flask, and explain, given that

149
00:06:54,900 --> 00:06:57,860
the two acids have different pH values.

150
00:06:58,020 --> 00:06:59,300
Pause here to answer.

151
00:07:09,700 --> 00:07:12,780
Both need twenty five point zero millilitres.

152
00:07:13,060 --> 00:07:15,620
Each acid gives one proton and reacts one

153
00:07:15,700 --> 00:07:18,420
to one, and both flasks hold the same

154
00:07:18,500 --> 00:07:20,500
two point five zero times ten to the

155
00:07:20,580 --> 00:07:22,100
minus three moles.

156
00:07:22,420 --> 00:07:26,660
Ethanoic acid starts mostly un-ionised, but as hydroxide

157
00:07:26,780 --> 00:07:30,580
removes hydronium, more molecules ionise, until all of

158
00:07:30,620 --> 00:07:32,100
